1m52|n|The relation or adaptation of one portion to another, or to the whole, as respect magnitude, quantity, or degree; comparative relation; ratio; as, the proportion of the parts of a building, or of the body. ; Harmonic relation between parts, or between different things of the same kind; symmetrical arrangement or adjustment; symmetry; as, to be out of proportion. ; The portion one receives when a whole is distributed by a rule or principle; equal or proper share; lot. ; A part considered comparatively; a share. ; The equality or similarity of ratios, especially of geometrical ratios; or a relation among quantities such that the quotient of the first divided by the second is equal to that of the third divided by the fourth; -- called also geometrical proportion, in distinction from arithmetical proportion, or that in which the difference of the first and second is equal to the difference of the third and fourth. ; The rule of three, in arithmetic, in which the three given terms, together with the one sought, are proportional.	a:1v0u,93,4;h6c,74,5;1308,72,5;1c5f,67,4;f0i,61,5;1yy6,57,6;1r3n,52,5;26re,49,3;22ft,48,6;i3a,47,6;p31,43,4;1z5z,40,4;7mq,40,5;1f2z,39,5;1oc3,38,6~1vhw,19,7;1593,23,7;1yy6,57,6;22ft,48,6;bn5,25,6;i3a,47,6;1unl,35,6;1oc3,38,6;1308,72,5;f0i,61,5;1f2z,39,5;h6c,74,5;7mq,40,5;1khj,38,5;1r3n,52,5	v:phg,57,3;1dga,46,3;10ti,37,3;qc2,22,2;uun,5,2~phg,57,3;10ti,37,3;1dga,46,3;uun,5,2;qc2,22,2	n:8ea,7,1~8ea,7,1
