1mby|n|A sea god in the service of Neptune who assumed different shapes at will. Hence, one who easily changes his appearance or principles. ; A genus of aquatic eel-shaped amphibians found in caves in Austria. They have permanent external gills as well as lungs. The eyes are small and the legs are weak. ; A changeable protozoan; an amoeba.	v:1249,32,9;26eh,16,4;26ev,13,3~1249,32,9;26eh,16,4;26ev,13,3	n:2nf,122,3~2nf,122,3	N:13ct,137,4;1utd,94,6;1utc,92,5;1wk3,85,4;ny9,71,3~1utd,94,6;1utc,92,5;13ct,137,4;1wk3,85,4;ny9,71,3
